/T (Proof of Non-regularity:  1. Choose w = a^p where p is a prime number > n  2. By the pumping lemma, w = xyz with |y| = m >= 1 and |xy| <= n  3. Then xy^i z = a^\(p+\(i-1\)m\)  4. For i = p+1: |xy^i z| = p + pm = p\(1+m\)  5. Since p is prime and \(1+m\) >= 2, p\(1+m\) is composite  6. Therefore, xy^i z is not in L for i = p+1 )
/E (Proof of Non-regularity:  1. Choose w = a^p where p is a prime number > n  2. By the pumping lemma, w = xyz with |y| = m >= 1 and |xy| <= n  3. Then xy^i z = a^\(p+\(i-1\)m\)  4. For i = p+1: |xy^i z| = p + pm = p\(1+m\)  5. Since p is prime and \(1+m\) >= 2, p\(1+m\) is composite  6. Therefore, xy^i z is not in L for i = p+1 )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [6]
