308 0 obj
<<
/Title (QUESTION 1  Smart Security System for Research Laboratory  Problem Statement:  A company is developing a smart security system for a research laboratory. Every employee entering  the lab uses a digital access card that generates a sequence of symbols:  a -> Valid ID scan  b -> Biometric verification  c -> Door access confirmation  The security rule states that:  1. Every valid access sequence must start with a  2. It may contain any number of biometric checks \(b\)  3. The sequence must end with c  Examples of valid sequences: ac, abc, abbc, abbbc  Solution:  Language Definition:  The language can be defined as: L = { a b^n c | n >= 0 }  Where:  'a' occurs exactly once at the beginning  'b' can occur zero or more times  'c' occurs exactly once at the end  Regular Expression:  R = a b* c  Finite Automaton \(NFA/DFA\):  The DFA for this language has the following states:  q0 \(Start state\) -> Reading 'a' transitions to q1  q1 \(Intermediate state\) -> Reading 'b' stays in q1, reading 'c' transitions to q2  q2 \(Final/Accepting state\) -> No further transitions)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 272 0 R
/Next 350 0 R
>>
endobj
309 0 obj
<<
/Title (Pumping Lemma: If L is regular, there exists n > 0 such that for any w in L with |w| >= n, we can write w = xyz where:  1. |xy| <= n  2. |y| >= 1  3. For all i >= 0, xy^i z in L)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 351 0 R
/Next 273 0 R
>>
endobj
